      "description": "Initial role with GTA, in 2001, as a mainframe programmer to process the state’s long distance usage gradually shifted in 2005 with 75% of time in the role of a SharePoint Site Collection Administrator/Developer for GTA’s Intranet, team sites and external hosted sites. \n\nAs a Site Collection Administrator of SP2003, and later a MOSS 2007 environment,\nmy duties were to:\n• Create and design SharePoint web sites/pages \n• Create/administer security permission levels and groups\n• Create training material and conduct training workshops \n• Provide direct support to end-users to resolve issues with SharePoint access and administration\n• Create customized workflows using SharePoint Designer; and\n• Design, develop and publish browser-enabled InfoPath forms.\n\nSince the first of 2014, being the member of a SharePoint 2013 Project team has involved gathering requirements and implementing a plan to replace the SharePoint 2007 environment with a SharePoint 2013 solution. Now as a Site Collection Administrator of three site collections in SP2013, my main role is to:\n• Create, design and customize SharePoint web sites/pages; and \n• Ensure the functionality of a number of InfoPath-based applications.",
      "insights": ""
     }
    ]
